WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.523
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:04.793 --> 00:07.085
Time to eat.

3
00:11.275 --> 00:12.600
Hey.

4
00:13.526 --> 00:15.172
Is that enough food?

5
00:15.172 --> 00:17.933
Yeah, it's enough.

6
00:19.969 --> 00:23.441
You always eat so much, Taguchi.

7
00:24.987 --> 00:27.947
But I've never had that from the convenience store before.

8
00:27.947 --> 00:28.980
Seriously?

9
00:28.980 --> 00:30.380
Yeah.

10
00:39.830 --> 00:41.219
Here.

11
00:56.283 --> 00:57.514
Good, right?

12
00:57.514 --> 00:58.874
Yeah!

13
01:01.498 --> 01:02.645
- Mr. Inoue. - Yes?

14
01:02.645 --> 01:05.290
This is Mr. Taguchi, the new engineer stationed here.

15
01:05.290 --> 01:07.742
Nice to meet you. I'm Inoue from Sales &amp; Planning.

16
01:07.742 --> 01:09.470
I'm Taguchi. Pleased to meet you.

17
01:09.470 --> 01:11.085
Likewise.

18
01:11.085 --> 01:12.772
Ms. Ohata.

19
01:12.772 --> 01:16.071
This is Mr. Taguchi, who'll be stationed here starting today.

20
01:16.071 --> 01:19.079
I'm Taguchi. Pleased to meet you.

21
01:19.079 --> 01:22.276
I'm Ohata. Nice to meet you.

22
01:22.902 --> 01:24.918
Thank you.

23
01:24.918 --> 01:26.245
Let's continue.

24
01:29.608 --> 01:31.186
Oh, Ms. Yamane.

25
01:31.186 --> 01:33.159
- Yes? - Well...

26
01:34.779 --> 01:38.736
This usage application form...

27
01:38.736 --> 01:41.450
Where do I get one?

28
01:41.450 --> 01:45.645
There's an application form for that, so I'll send it to you later.

29
01:49.843 --> 01:51.796
Let's eat.

30
01:52.802 --> 01:55.645
You still eat so little.

31
01:55.645 --> 01:57.342
Yeah.

32
01:57.342 --> 02:00.755
You're eating a lot, as always, huh?

33
02:00.755 --> 02:02.102
Yeah.

34
02:09.248 --> 02:10.688
Want some?

35
02:14.156 --> 02:18.398
I'm an adult now, so I'll pass.

36
02:20.317 --> 02:22.532
Where should I put this?

37
02:38.867 --> 02:41.127
What do you mean, an adult?

38
02:42.243 --> 02:45.167
It's nothing.

39
04:10.761 --> 04:15.008
Hey, you should stop doing that kind of thing.

40
04:16.233 --> 04:18.311
What kind of thing?

41
04:19.454 --> 04:21.101
I mean...

42
04:24.609 --> 04:27.077
Never mind. It's nothing.

43
04:29.320 --> 04:31.332
Should you really be here?

44
04:31.332 --> 04:34.124
I bet you can make friends easily.

45
04:41.323 --> 04:44.396
So is it better if I don't come?

46
04:47.873 --> 04:49.759
Do whatever you want.

47
04:50.876 --> 04:53.521
I feel at ease here.

48
05:03.237 --> 05:06.185
[Yamane]

49
05:07.324 --> 05:11.892
Taguchi? The one with blond hair and piercings?

50
05:12.506 --> 05:13.926
Yeah.

51
05:14.779 --> 05:16.576
Is he still blond?

52
05:16.576 --> 05:19.755
No, his hair is black now.

53
05:19.755 --> 05:23.501
Didn't he have a ton of piercings in both ears?

54
05:23.501 --> 05:25.159
You remember well.

55
05:25.159 --> 05:29.173
Because back then, you talked about Taguchi every day.

56
05:30.447 --> 05:32.314
Did I?

57
05:35.737 --> 05:38.208
That's amazing.

58
05:38.208 --> 05:41.105
A reunion after ten years...

59
05:42.713 --> 05:46.708
Since you got to meet again, why not go out for a meal?

60
05:47.681 --> 05:52.292
We had lunch together, but that was at work.

61
05:53.625 --> 05:55.565
And besides...

62
05:58.487 --> 06:01.469
I feel restless around him.

63
06:02.987 --> 06:06.999
Oh? Restless, huh?

64
06:17.672 --> 06:19.977
I finished the cooperation request form.

65
06:19.977 --> 06:23.090
Thanks. I'll check it later.

66
06:24.865 --> 06:27.236
Also, I'm sorry.

67
06:27.236 --> 06:28.742
For what?

68
06:28.742 --> 06:31.182
For taking so long.

69
06:35.738 --> 06:40.534
Are you a bit tired?

70
06:40.534 --> 06:42.233
Huh?

71
06:42.233 --> 06:44.729
You've been doing new tasks lately.

72
06:45.752 --> 06:48.338
Which meeting record do you mean?

73
06:48.338 --> 06:51.207
I believe it was from the interim report.

74
06:51.207 --> 06:53.010
Understood. I'll check.

75
06:53.010 --> 06:54.597
Thank you.

76
07:03.292 --> 07:05.258
Ms. Yamane?

77
07:05.258 --> 07:10.017
Thank you for your concern, but I'll do my best.

78
07:16.050 --> 07:18.165
That's tough.

79
07:18.165 --> 07:19.737
Huh?

80
07:19.737 --> 07:24.803
I hope there's a high school that accepts our request to do a field test.

81
07:25.798 --> 07:27.445
Yeah.

82
07:33.704 --> 07:37.997
[The Regsarkana Sovereignty] And that's what happened in Chapter One.

83
07:37.997 --> 07:40.190
Oh?

84
07:48.461 --> 07:50.459
I pushed this book onto you,

85
07:50.459 --> 07:53.713
and you're gonna read it soon too.

86
07:53.713 --> 07:56.148
I'm sorry for the spoilers.

87
07:56.148 --> 07:57.583
I got a little carried away.

88
07:57.583 --> 07:59.923
No, it's fine.

89
07:59.923 --> 08:02.245
I don't usually read books anyway.

90
08:02.245 --> 08:06.239
It's easier to read when you explain it like that.

91
08:12.352 --> 08:14.012
What happens next?

92
08:16.218 --> 08:20.206
In Chapter Two, a character I really love shows up.

93
08:20.206 --> 08:23.181
He's a bit like you, Taguchi.

94
08:23.181 --> 08:28.162
Right, if I had to say what I like about him exactly...

95
08:28.162 --> 08:30.270
That's a bit embarrassing, so don't tell me.

96
08:30.270 --> 08:32.213
Huh?

97
08:32.213 --> 08:33.696
Why?

98
08:34.407 --> 08:36.155
"Why"?

99
08:40.747 --> 08:42.849
I should get going.

100
08:42.849 --> 08:44.189
Huh?

101
08:46.212 --> 08:47.692
To class.

102
08:51.096 --> 08:53.175
What is it?

103
08:53.175 --> 08:54.850
Well...

104
08:54.850 --> 09:00.499
It's just that... fun times really fly by.

105
09:00.499 --> 09:02.519
We have tomorrow anyway.

106
09:03.711 --> 09:08.257
Tomorrow, I have an English vocab test fifth period,

107
09:08.257 --> 09:10.579
so I need to study at lunchtime.

108
09:22.495 --> 09:23.908
What?

109
09:25.957 --> 09:27.117
Ow...

110
09:29.049 --> 09:31.562
I might be here after school too.

111
09:32.366 --> 09:33.719
Oh...

112
09:35.887 --> 09:37.735
See you tomorrow.

113
09:40.115 --> 09:41.935
See you tomorrow!

114
09:55.776 --> 09:58.638
[Taguchi: Can I show you something on a video call today?]

115
10:21.061 --> 10:23.977
This angle is a bit low.

116
10:35.527 --> 10:37.327
And then...

117
10:39.922 --> 10:41.955
Good, that works.

118
10:49.388 --> 10:51.527
Sorry to keep you waiting!

119
10:51.527 --> 10:53.542
Wait, are you working?

120
10:54.696 --> 10:56.240
Sorry.

121
11:00.916 --> 11:03.603
You wear glasses at home?

122
11:04.371 --> 11:07.142
Yeah, is it weird?

123
11:07.142 --> 11:10.985
Oh, no, it just feels new to me.

124
11:11.663 --> 11:14.831
So, what was it you wanted to show me?

125
11:14.831 --> 11:16.650
Oh, right.

126
11:17.515 --> 11:18.640
This.

127
11:18.640 --> 11:22.150
[The Regsarkana Sovereignty] Is that a new release?

128
11:22.150 --> 11:23.851
Yeah.

129
11:23.851 --> 11:26.379
The same series you gave me.

130
11:27.043 --> 11:30.293
But you said you don't read books.

131
11:30.293 --> 11:33.582
You're the reason I started reading, Yamane.

132
11:33.582 --> 11:34.829
Huh?

133
11:37.396 --> 11:41.374
Right. You said a character you like resembles me?

134
11:42.267 --> 11:44.807
Yeah, he's like you, Taguchi.

135
11:44.807 --> 11:46.789
Why do you like him?

136
11:49.555 --> 11:52.108
Well...

137
11:56.567 --> 12:00.439
I can't really put it into words.

138
12:01.866 --> 12:03.372
I see.

139
12:05.649 --> 12:09.649
How about lately? Read any interesting novels?

140
12:10.825 --> 12:13.658
Lately? Let me think.

141
12:15.115 --> 12:16.197
Yeah, so then,

142
12:16.197 --> 12:22.419
he wakes up in a lighthouse, which is so interesting to me.

143
12:24.902 --> 12:28.362
I'm so sorry! I spoiled it again.

144
12:28.362 --> 12:32.472
No, it's fun hearing your explanations.

145
12:32.472 --> 12:35.156
You're just a good listener, Taguchi.

146
12:35.156 --> 12:36.708
I see.

147
12:40.009 --> 12:42.776
It's already so late.

148
12:42.776 --> 12:45.420
Oh, you're right.

149
12:47.579 --> 12:51.197
It's late today, so I should probably go.

150
12:51.197 --> 12:54.364
Oh, right! Sorry for keeping you up.

151
12:54.364 --> 12:55.377
Well then...

152
12:55.377 --> 12:58.771
Wait, Yamane.

153
12:58.771 --> 13:00.172
What?

154
13:01.408 --> 13:04.323
I couldn't say it yesterday or today, but...

155
13:06.901 --> 13:08.553
See you tomorrow.

156
13:14.344 --> 13:16.215
See you tomorrow.

157
13:33.577 --> 13:35.991
See you tomorrow.

158
13:50.753 --> 13:52.634
Good work.

159
13:53.300 --> 13:55.534
Good work.

160
14:13.379 --> 14:15.619
Wanna get lunch together?

161
14:17.760 --> 14:19.133
Sure.

162
14:30.431 --> 14:32.031
Seriously?

163
14:32.897 --> 14:34.864
What's wrong?

164
14:34.864 --> 14:36.726
Our parent company emailed us.

165
14:36.726 --> 14:40.192
They want a detailed offerings report within the day.

166
14:40.192 --> 14:41.278
What?

167
14:41.278 --> 14:43.864
But they said that was next week.

168
14:43.864 --> 14:46.362
There isn't enough time today.

169
14:48.490 --> 14:50.657
If it's tough, I can help.

170
14:50.657 --> 14:52.685
I can't let you do that.

171
14:54.669 --> 14:56.515
I'll help too.

172
14:56.515 --> 14:59.296
But what about your own work, Ms. Yamane?

173
14:59.296 --> 15:03.097
Mine can definitely wait till tomorrow.

174
15:03.097 --> 15:06.020
I don't know if I can be useful, but...

175
15:07.185 --> 15:09.473
You're right.

176
15:09.473 --> 15:12.080
Let's all do it together.

177
15:12.080 --> 15:14.861
But first, I'll go talk to the parent company people.

178
15:14.861 --> 15:16.001
Huh?

179
15:16.001 --> 15:20.738
We'll make a proper draft, but I'll adjust their expectations.

180
15:20.738 --> 15:22.744
Thank you.

181
15:26.049 --> 15:28.565
Does she think I'm unreliable?

182
15:28.565 --> 15:30.319
Huh?

183
15:30.319 --> 15:33.254
I think she's just being considerate.

184
15:33.991 --> 15:36.067
I hope so.

185
15:37.092 --> 15:39.560
For now, I'll forward the email to you.

186
15:39.560 --> 15:41.288
- Okay. - Thank you.

187
15:41.288 --> 15:42.809
No problem.

188
15:50.869 --> 15:57.575
[Urgent work. Can't come. I'm really sorry.]

189
16:21.192 --> 16:31.613
[It's okay. Do your best!]

190
16:45.905 --> 16:48.365
[The Regsarkana Sovereignty]

191
16:57.626 --> 16:59.762
You seem happy today, Yamane.

192
16:59.762 --> 17:00.796
Huh?

193
17:00.796 --> 17:02.629
Did something good happen?

194
17:03.677 --> 17:07.716
Well, there's something I'm kind of looking forward to after this.

195
17:07.716 --> 17:09.238
Is that so?

196
17:09.238 --> 17:14.290
Well, there's hardly any work left, so you can go home for today.

197
17:15.131 --> 17:16.816
Thank you!

198
17:16.816 --> 17:19.344
Then I'll head out first.

199
17:23.104 --> 17:25.271
Good work.

200
17:26.296 --> 17:28.161
Huh?

201
17:28.161 --> 17:29.945
Is something wrong?

202
17:29.945 --> 17:33.971
The book title and barcode info don't match.

203
17:33.971 --> 17:36.419
Maybe they were stuck on the wrong data.

204
17:36.419 --> 17:41.388
A bunch of books came in at once the other day.

205
17:42.018 --> 17:44.935
We'll need to redo them all.

206
17:49.166 --> 17:51.139
I'll do it.

207
17:51.139 --> 17:52.192
You will?

208
17:52.192 --> 17:55.182
I don't have practice today, so I'm free.

209
17:56.422 --> 17:58.848
Yamane, see you.

210
18:02.744 --> 18:04.411
See you tomorrow.

211
18:11.241 --> 18:12.656
Wait.

212
18:12.656 --> 18:15.049
[Send]

213
18:15.049 --> 18:16.449
[Sent]

214
18:18.044 --> 18:20.704
Done!

215
18:23.940 --> 18:26.327
Thank you so much!

216
18:26.327 --> 18:28.548
It was nothing, really.

217
18:28.548 --> 18:30.019
No worries.

218
18:30.019 --> 18:31.798
It's late, so let's hurry home.

219
18:31.798 --> 18:33.824
- Okay. - Got it.

220
18:36.991 --> 18:40.255
By the way, an approval email for the field test came in.

221
18:40.255 --> 18:41.744
Huh, already?

222
18:41.744 --> 18:44.888
Yes, isn't that great?

223
18:46.687 --> 18:51.105
The school that emailed us is this one.

224
18:51.105 --> 18:52.328
Huh?

225
18:53.316 --> 18:55.236
It's my Alma mater.

226
18:55.236 --> 18:56.583
What?

227
18:57.326 --> 19:01.136
I knew it was on our list, but...

228
19:01.136 --> 19:02.971
I see.

229
19:03.658 --> 19:06.541
I'd like to visit my own school too.

230
19:06.541 --> 19:08.487
Was your school around here?

231
19:08.487 --> 19:10.274
No, it's in Nagoya.

232
19:14.770 --> 19:18.334
Excuse me, I'll be heading out now.

233
19:19.839 --> 19:22.190
- Good work. - Good work!

234
20:05.277 --> 20:07.038
Taguchi.

235
20:09.266 --> 20:11.053
Yamane?

236
20:12.307 --> 20:14.105
Thank goodness.

237
20:14.105 --> 20:15.798
You're still here.

238
20:19.024 --> 20:21.482
My meeting ran long too.

239
20:22.609 --> 20:24.509
I see.

240
20:29.310 --> 20:30.831
What?

241
20:31.980 --> 20:34.464
Did you want to see me that badly?

242
20:40.618 --> 20:42.025
Yeah.

243
20:48.736 --> 20:52.872
After you said, "see you tomorrow",

244
20:53.982 --> 20:56.349
I was just so anxious.

245
21:01.160 --> 21:04.174
Not just today,

246
21:05.917 --> 21:07.570
but back then too.

247
21:10.509 --> 21:11.869
Huh?

248
21:18.562 --> 21:22.241
Being together is fun,

249
21:23.192 --> 21:27.561
and it's hard to wait till we meet again.

250
21:29.563 --> 21:32.026
Even when I was alone,

251
21:33.110 --> 21:36.586
I'd think about the stuff that made me laugh

252
21:36.586 --> 21:41.355
or what we'd talk about tomorrow.

253
21:41.355 --> 21:44.859
It was always on my mind.

254
21:51.428 --> 21:57.470
So being able to say "see you tomorrow" to you again,

255
21:57.470 --> 22:00.387
like back then,

256
22:02.909 --> 22:05.296
makes me really happy.

257
22:10.690 --> 22:15.631
Sorry. What am I even saying?

258
22:17.797 --> 22:19.284
Bye, then.

259
22:29.434 --> 22:31.418
Today, I...

260
22:33.577 --> 22:35.462
I was anxious too.

261
22:37.416 --> 22:38.783
Huh?

262
22:43.879 --> 22:45.883
We only had a few months together...

263
22:48.583 --> 22:51.416
ten years ago,

264
22:56.297 --> 22:59.681
but I just couldn't forget about you, Yamane.

265
23:14.933 --> 23:16.534
I like you.

266
23:22.278 --> 23:24.439
I've always liked you.

267
23:34.166 --> 23:36.024
Will you...

268
23:37.641 --> 23:39.761
go out with me?

269
23:45.004 --> 23:46.643
If things go wrong,

270
23:46.643 --> 23:48.924
I feel like we can't even go back to being friends.

271
23:48.924 --> 23:51.554
Let's ask Taguchi out on a date.

272
23:51.554 --> 23:54.814
If it's too much for you, we can just stay friends like before.

273
23:54.814 --> 23:57.721
Is that really okay with you, Taguchi?

274
23:57.721 --> 23:59.934
I want to get closer to you.
